      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "From 1880 to 1932, Penhook was a stop on the Franklin & Pittsylvania Railroad, linking Rocky Mount to Gretna.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://smithmountainlake.com/lifestyles/the-people-of-penhook/article_6413097f-dccf-5c4f-9039-a3ae8c5a43b4.html",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Penhook borders the Cool Branch arm of Smith Mountain Lake, placing it on the lake’s eastern edge.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
